From: Brian 'redbeard' Harrington <redbeard@dead-city.org>
Subject: [PATCH] spacemit: suspend dispatch, type-0 WFI, error propagation, P0-4 context audit

Implementation batches P0 (1-3) and P0-4/5 per the suspend-ownership
plan. All disassembly-verified.

P0-1 EXPLICIT DISPATCH: type 0 -> plain wfi; 0x80000000 -> ENOTSUPP;
0x90000000 -> ENOTSUPP (see P0-4 F6); cluster -> ENOTSUPP (gated on
the ESOS P1 model); anything else -> EINVAL BEFORE any hardware
change.

P0-2 GENUINE DEFAULT-RETENTIVE: type 0 = wfi() before votes,
masking, IMSIC, cache changes.

P0-3 ERROR PROPAGATION: the K3 wrapper returns the backend result
(failures logged with hart/type/error).

P0-4 CONTEXT AUDIT (docs/p0-4-context-audit-2026-11-20.md):
F1/F4  vote/devote are now a NAMED pair: spacemit_devote_pwrdown_core
       added as the exact inverse of the vote (the historical unmask
       cleared the vote by accident); k3_hsm_cleanup_wake() is the
       single documented cleanup owner for future wake/abort paths.
F2     the pending-interrupt check is folded INTO
       __rpmi_hsm_suspend (abort with SBI_EFAIL + flags=1 before the
       first CSR write) — previously only the unenforced _pre() had
       it, so a direct caller could tear the IMSIC save.
F3     HSTATUS restored after the VGEN sweep (virtual-interrupt
       routing intact on in-place wake).
F5     csi_enable_data_preftch() added as the named inverse; the
       wake path previously never re-enabled prefetch.
F6     0x90000000 REJECTED: its in-place wake restores neither IMSIC
       nor H-state nor vote nor prefetch while the SBI non-retentive
       contract expects warmboot resume — the resume contract is
       unresolved, so no non-retentive state is offered until one is
       implemented and qualified (the P0-6 principle). The defective
       vote+WFI path is DELETED, replaced by the cleanup-ownership
       table documenting the required pairings for the future
       qualified implementation.
F7     "for a100" comment corrected to x100.

The only offered suspend type is the qualified retentive type-0 WFI.

Build identity: fw_dynamic.bin sha256
c83ce98ee4efe897a6da91d7b933a4ce67e1f00edbad095a64c222110f345e46
(269920 bytes). Disassembly: type-0 = 'wfi; ret'; pending check
('csrr stopei/mtopei; bnez -> flags=1, li a0,-1') precedes the first
CSR write; HSTATUS restore ('ld ...1064(a6); csrw hstatus') follows
the VGEN sweep; every non-retentive type exits to 'li a0,-2' before
the vote.

HARDWARE QUALIFICATION (acceptance): timer/IPI/UART wake from type
0; no votes/cache/snoop changes on type 0; rejected types return
errors with no hardware change; with virtualization active, per-hart
repeated type-0 suspend/resume preserves execution and interrupt
delivery.

--- a/include/sbi_utils/cache/cache.h
+++ b/include/sbi_utils/cache/cache.h
@@ static inline void csi_disable_data_preftch(void)
+static inline void csi_enable_data_preftch(void)
+{ csr_set(CSR_MSETUP, 32); }

--- a/lib/utils/hsm/fdt_hsm_rpmi.c
+++ b/lib/utils/hsm/fdt_hsm_rpmi.c
@@ static int rpmi_hsm_suspend(u32 type, ulong resume_addr)
+	int rc = __rpmi_hsm_suspend(type);
+	if (rc) sbi_printf("rpmi-hsm: hart %u suspend type %#x failed: %d\n", ...);
+	return rc;

--- a/platform/generic/spacemit/k3_corepm.c
+++ b/platform/generic/spacemit/k3_corepm.c
@@ int __rpmi_hsm_suspend(u32 type)
+	if (type == SBI_HSM_SUSPEND_RET_DEFAULT) { wfi(); return 0; }
+	[F2: pending STOPEI/MTOPEI check -> flags=1, SBI_EFAIL]
 	[IMSIC M/S save]
 	[H-state save + VGEN sweep]
+	[F3: csr_write(CSR_HSTATUS, imsic->hstatus) after the sweep]
+	[F6: all non-retentive types -> SBI_ENOTSUPP; the vote+WFI
+	 path deleted; k3_hsm_cleanup_wake() documents the P0-5
+	 entry/cleanup pairings]
+void spacemit_devote_pwrdown_core(uint32_t hartid)  [F1/F4 inverse]

HARDWARE-VALIDATED FIXES (v14/v15 phase-A wedges; docs/v14-phaseA-findings.md):

Dispatch hoist (v15): type validation moved to the TOP of
__rpmi_hsm_suspend, before the pending-check + IRQ mask + IMSIC
save. Previously a rejected type returned with FI interrupts
masked and IMSIC half-saved. Zero CSR/PMU writes on rejection
(disassembly-verified). Necessary but not sufficient alone.

ENOTSUPP fallback translation (v16): sbi_hsm_hart_suspend()
consumes SBI_ENOTSUPP from a DEFAULT suspend type as a request to
run the GENERIC implementation (plain wfi), then for
non-retentive types jumps to the warm-boot entry to simulate
resume — on this platform re-running K3 PMA/L2/snoop init with
MIE cleared and parking the hart permanently (hard lockup, no
NMI; both v14 hart 4 and v15 hart 7 wedged exactly this way).
The wrapper now translates ENOTSUPP + NON_RET_DEFAULT into
SBI_EFAIL so the ecall fails outright. Platform-defined types
pass ENOTSUPP through unchanged (the generic fallback only
applies to the two default types).

--- a/lib/utils/hsm/fdt_hsm_rpmi.c  (v16 addition)
@@ static int rpmi_hsm_suspend(u32 type, ulong resume_addr)
 	rc = __rpmi_hsm_suspend(type);
 	if (rc)
 		sbi_printf("rpmi-hsm: hart %u suspend type %#x failed: %d\n", ...);
+	if (rc == SBI_ENOTSUPP && type == SBI_HSM_SUSPEND_NON_RET_DEFAULT)
+		return SBI_EFAIL;
 	return rc;

CLUSTER-RETENTIVE ROUTING (v21, P1 activation):

New platform type K3_HSM_SUSP_CLUSTER_RET (0x11000000, retentive bit
clear — in-place resume, no warmboot contract). The type is routed
through RPMI_HSM_SRV_HART_SUSPEND (k3_rpmi_hsm_route_suspend in
fdt_hsm_rpmi.c: per-hart chan from the rpmi-hsm probe, inline
advertised-type check against the ESOS suspend table, synchronous
bounded request) so the ESOS ownership gate DRIVES the decision:

  deny  (RPMI_ERR_DENIED / timeout / unknown type / transport)
        -> error to the SBI caller, ZERO hardware change
  grant (domain COMMITTED)
        -> vote + WFI + devote on the affected hart; no cache, snoop,
           or IMSIC operations — full architectural retention

ESOS side: rcpu DT gains the cluster-retentive@18 idle-state
(sbi-suspend-param 0x11000000) so the service table accepts the type;
no ESOS code change (the existing P1 prepare gate + bounded
k3_domain_request_sleep run on receipt).

NOT advertised in _LPI until hardware-qualified (P0-6 principle);
the test module drives it first.

--- a/lib/utils/hsm/fdt_hsm_rpmi.c  (v21 addition)
@@ K3 branch
+int k3_rpmi_hsm_route_suspend(u32 type, ulong resume_addr)
+{
+	struct rpmi_hsm_hart_susp_req req;
+	struct rpmi_hsm_hart_susp_resp resp;
+	struct rpmi_hsm *rpmi = rpmi_hsm_get_pointer(current_hartid());
+	int i;
+
+	if (!rpmi || !rpmi->chan)
+		return SBI_ENODEV;
+	for (i = 0; i < rpmi->susp->num_states; i++)
+		if (rpmi->susp->states[i].suspend_param == type)
+			break;
+	if (i >= rpmi->susp->num_states)
+		return SBI_ENOTSUPP;
+	req.hartid = current_hartid();
+	req.suspend_type = type;
+	req.resume_addr_lo = resume_addr;
+	req.resume_addr_hi = (u64)resume_addr >> 32;
+	return rpmi_normal_request_with_status(...);
+}

--- a/platform/generic/spacemit/k3_corepm.c  (v21 addition)
@@ dispatch (after the type-0 WFI early return)
+	if (type == K3_HSM_SUSP_CLUSTER_RET) {
+		int rc = k3_rpmi_hsm_route_suspend(type, 0);
+		if (rc)
+			return rc;
+		spacemit_vote_powrdown_core(current_hartid());
+		wfi();
+		spacemit_devote_pwrdown_core(current_hartid());
+		return 0;
+	}

Disassembly-verified: the 0x11000000 branch calls the routing before
any CSR read or MMIO write; a nonzero routing return exits through
the epilogue with no mhartid read and no vote; only success reaches
csrr mhartid -> vote -> wfi -> devote.
